From 33b3010bf35feef5deb911fee5f4e20049166bf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cameron Bytheway <bythewc@amazon.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 23:39:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rcdzc: pin abstract-type opacity depth-recursion + value-hold
 boundary gate cases
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two coverage cases in 11-modules.sexp pinning the exact scope of the CDZ0202
abstract-key/element opacity reject:
- a Map keyed by a deeply-nested compound (Tuple (Tuple Temp Int64) Int64) with
  the abstract leaf two tuples deep still rejects — opacity recurses to any depth.
- an abstract value held as a Map VALUE under a concrete key is LEGAL — opacity
  rejects only the KEY-comparison observation, never a hold-don't-compare value.

Both pin existing behavior against a future shallow-walk or over-reach regression.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 spec/semantics/.gate-baseline            |  2 ++
 spec/semantics/.gate-baseline-rust       |  2 ++
 spec/semantics/.gate-baseline-rust-async |  2 ++
 spec/semantics/11-modules.sexp           | 45 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 51 insertions(+)

diff --git a/spec/semantics/.gate-baseline b/spec/semantics/.gate-baseline
index 678631067..f1b8ab1a3 100644
--- a/spec/semantics/.gate-baseline
+++ b/spec/semantics/.gate-baseline
@@ -5426,6 +5426,8 @@ pass	a Map keyed by a COMPOUND containing an abstract type is rejected (opacity
 pass	Set.to-list over Option elements enumerates Some-first per the declared order
 pass	a built-in comparison on a COMPOUND containing an abstract type is rejected (opacity walks the compound)
 pass	a Set/Map lookup over an abstract-element collection reached via a param is rejected (read-side opacity)
+pass	a Map keyed by a DEEPLY-nested compound containing an abstract type is rejected (opacity recurses to any depth)
+pass	an abstract-typed value held as a Map VALUE under a concrete key is legal (value-holding never triggers the opacity reject)
 pass	Record.extend chained onto Record.without of a map-borne record computes, not traps
 pass	the same without-extend chain on a LIST-borne record computes
 pass	single row ops on a map-borne record compute — without alone and extend alone
